                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "There are going to be a lot of changed lines in the next set to support the yielding D-Bus APIs, so this was not yet a thorough review. But enough to keep things moving."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 114,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "this should be unnecessary if you use the yielding D-Bus APIs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 114,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anirudh Tiwari",
                        "email": "Anirudh.Tiwari@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "antiwar_microsoft"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. The dbusConn() singleton and the standalone service-discovery helper are gone. resolveService(ctx, \u2026) now uses the yielding ipmi::getService(ctx, intf, path, out) overload and is shared by all four call sites."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 164,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "I think I would prefer actually handling the other values appropriately than an abort or whatever __builtin_unreachable does. At the very least throwing an exception will unwind the handler and return an IPMI error code. Since an invalid enum is unlikely a fatal error, let's not treat it as one."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 164,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anirudh Tiwari",
                        "email": "Anirudh.Tiwari@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "antiwar_microsoft"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. The pefUnreachable() helper is removed and both ccFor() / mapErr<>() switches now fall through to responseUnspecifiedError() (CC 0xFF). An unexpected DbusResult value surfaces to the IPMI client as a generic error instead of aborting the handler thread."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 261,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "If a D-Bus call is made from ipmi handler context, it must use the yielding D-Bus APIs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 261,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anirudh Tiwari",
                        "email": "Anirudh.Tiwari@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "antiwar_microsoft"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. dbusGetByteProp(ctx, \u2026) uses ctx->bus->yield_method_call<std::variant<uint8_t>>(ctx->yield, ec, \u2026)."
                },
                {
