                        "username": "antiwar_microsoft"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Signature is now ipmiGetPefConfigParams(ipmi::Context::ptr ctx, uint8_t paramSelByte, uint8_t setSelector, uint8_t blockSelector)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.hpp",
                    "line": 100,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "Are any of these values expected to be used in other cpp files? If not, just roll these into the top of the pefhandler.cpp file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.hpp",
                    "line": 100,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anirudh Tiwari",
                        "email": "Anirudh.Tiwari@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "antiwar_microsoft"
                    },
                    "message": "Pushing back on consistency + extensibility grounds, happy to fold if you'd still prefer:\n\nConsistency with peer handlers. chassishandler.hpp (40 LoC, 6 constants), dcmihandler.hpp (51 LoC, 23 constants), and transporthandler.hpp (450 LoC, 8 constants) all keep companion headers carrying command/parameter constants that no other .cpp in this repo includes. pefhandler.hpp follows the same split.\n\nDocumented D-Bus contract surface. The header also documents the PefManager / PefFilter interface contract (object paths, property names, byte layout of the 20-byte filter entry per IPMI 2.0 Table 17.7, pefMaxFilters slot count, ObjectManager requirements). The in-tree provider and the matcher  intentionally carry parallel local copies because they live in separate Yocto recipes that can't share a header, but they were authored against this contract.\n\nFuture use. Any in-tree provider, mock, or unit test added later naturally #includes the header rather than redefining the constants \u2014 that's the cheap insurance the header buys."
                }
            ],
