            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anirudh Tiwari",
                        "email": "Anirudh.Tiwari@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "antiwar_microsoft"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the PS1 review. PS2 addresses all inline comments and reworks the D-Bus layer to use the yielding APIs on\u00a0`ipmi::Context::ptr`. Tested on hardware : wire round-trips byte-identical, no timeouts/deadlocks in ipmid's journal under concurrent provider activity, CRUD/persistence/matcher/ghost/wrong-format/no-provider all green. Inline replies below."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this a new service that will be in upstream? Is it being included in another service like PIM, EM or whatsoever? Is there a design doc for it? I can't find any (submitted) design or code about PEF except for this CR. The mentioned D-Bus interface, as well as `PefFilter` are not published by any service yet."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "I haven't reviewed the D-Bus related code that much but it doesn't look right at all (lots of logic for things like D-Bus service state parsing which feels over-engineered.)\nUsually we have documented D-Bus interfaces for this in phosphor-dbus-interfaces which define how a message should look like, some of which also have a raw data field there.\n\nAdditionally, I don't get what `PefManager` and `PefFilter` will do here. There's no design doc for it anywhere, so it's unclear how ipmid has to interact with this service in the first place."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 60,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Use `lg2`, not `phosphor::logging`. Most of the code was already migrated to `lg2`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 67,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "How is a user supposed to configure this value otherwise? If it should be user-configurable then make sure to add a meson option, but I don't see why they should be able to do that in the first place."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "30-3 is the \"Arm PEF postpone timer command\". I _think_ you're referring to table `30-6` instead."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.hpp",
                    "line": 87,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "The reference you're mentioning here does not match with the spec (I've \ngot IPMI 2.0 rev 1.1 April 21, 2015 E7 Markup). What I see:\n\nbyte 9 + 10 = Event Data 1 Event Offset Mask\nbyte 11 = Event Data 1 AND Mask\nbyte 12 = Event Data 1 Compare 1\nbyte 13 = Event Data 1 Compare 2\n\nand the next bytes (14..19) are always \"Event Data N AND Mask\", \"Event \nData N Compare 1\" and \"Event Data N Compare 2\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.hpp",
                    "line": 88,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "not in this table entry. I've no clue where this is coming from."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.hpp",
                    "line": 89,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Part of byte 2 (Alert Policy Number) bites 6:4:\n\n> [6:4] - group control selector (1-based). Selects entry from group control table. (see [ICMB)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.hpp",
                    "line": 109,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "why do you assert on compile time for this value? This feels unnecessary."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pefhandler.hpp",
                    "line": 128,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "No use of `propRawData` anywhere here?"
                }
